%% Converting spike times to a matrix and extracting NREM spikes
% This script loads the detected spike times for all recorded cells and
% determines the maximum number of spikes among the cells. The cell-based
% spike-time data are then converted into a zero-padded matrix, where each
% column represents one cell and each row corresponds to a spike time.
% The resulting matrix is saved for subsequent analysis.
%
% The predefined NREM/SWS episode time intervals are used to create a
% sample-based logical index corresponding to all NREM periods. Spike times
% from each cell are mapped to the nearest EEG recording sample and
% converted into a binary spike-train representation.
%
% The spike trains are subsequently restricted to the NREM/SWS periods,
% producing a matrix containing the spike activity of all recorded cells
% exclusively during NREM episodes. The resulting NREM spike-train matrix
% is saved for subsequent neuronal activity analysis.

clc
clear 
close all
